r_duplicates ([]). Matrices [pork, meat] retained but flagged in Verification notes as outside standard matrices vocabulary (no closer match in system-prompt list). Ingest committed eabe4d1. Phase-2 fresh-context subagent verdict REVISE: 4 ⚠️ Check 1 (numerical fidelity) findings, 1 ⚠️ Check 2 (slug vocabulary) finding (downgraded by subagent itself from initial ❌), Checks 3/4/5 all ✅. Key Check 1 finding APPLIED: prior 'approximately 96-98% RE in CCLP at 20 kGy/150 ppm (Figure 2A)' misread the figure; paper Introduction (p. 1) explicitly states 'a reductive efficiency of approximately 80% for the free Cr(VI)' as the headline result, with 98.03% in Abstract being study-wide max across all panel/condition combinations (panel unspecified by authors); visual reading of Figure 2A at 20 kGy/150 ppm CCLP baseline sits in ~80-85% band, CCMP at same condition ~95%; stress-condition Figure 3 panels are where 95-98% bars sit. Revised Key numbers to: paper headline ~80%, study-wide max 98.03%, CCLP baseline ~80-85%, CCMP baseline ~95%. Check 2 finding REJECTED: pork-chop/pork-bacon flagged as loose mappings — verified both are in 2026-05-17 taxonomy snapshot AND mapping rationale (lean-pork/CCLP analog, fatty-pork/CCFP analog) is already documented in Verification notes; routing layer benefits from fan-out; retained without change. Three other Check 1 ⚠️ on visual-inference bar-chart reads (temperature band 87-96%, RCCLP band 78-87%, NaCl/pH ~95% hedge) acknowledged without change — wiki already discloses visual-inference basis, no source tabulation exists in PDF. Audit-application commit cb8e552. Routing clean (0 unresolved, 0 blocking malformed; advisory-only products[] which is correct for a methods/mitigation study not measuring specific products). 5 findings; 1 applied; 1 rejected; 3 acknowledged-without-change.; ['']"
