The results of this work may suggest that, depending on the
type of metal, the plant uses a remediation mechanism. These
findings align with other studies where L. perenne has been
employed as a phytoremediation plant. Previous authors have
demonstrated that L. perenne exhibits metabolic changes when
exposed to Cd2+ concentrations of 0.25 mg/L, while no
adverse effects were observed at concentrations exceeding 25
